// Title: Potential Perl Reverse Shell Execution
// ID: 259df6bc-003f-4306-9f54-4ff1a08fa38e
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: @d4ns4n_, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-04-07
// Tags: attack.execution
// Description: Detects execution of the perl binary with the "-e" flag and common strings related to potential reverse shell activity
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((((src.process.cmdline containsCIS "fdopen(" AND src.process.cmdline containsCIS "::Socket::INET")) OR ((src.process.cmdline containsCIS "Socket" AND src.process.cmdline containsCIS "connect" AND src.process.cmdline containsCIS "open" AND src.process.cmdline containsCIS "exec"))) AND (src.process.image.path endswithCIS "/perl" AND src.process.cmdline containsCIS " -e "))
